{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed. The second publish failed because populated-table similarity scores were Python floats, which DynamoDB rejects; the first publish had no existing stories and therefore no scores.\n\n- Converted related scores to integer percentages in `src/app.py:38`.\n- Added a regression test that publishes twice through `handler()` and verifies both return 201 in `tests/test_publish.py:27`.\n- Documented the cause, fix, and applicable parts of the colleague’s note in `ANSWER.md`.\n\nVerification: `python3 -m unittest discover tests` — **2 tests passed**."}
